<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$35 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$35 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Australian promissory note issuers held tenders on Friday, reaping a total of A$35 million from the commercial paper market.</p>
<p>ICI Australia made the largest issue, placing A$20 million of its paper at 2.5 to 3.5 basis points over the corresponding bank bill mid-rate.</p>
<p>The physical bank bill yield curve has returned to a normal shape with dealers reporting minimal turnover during morning trade.</p>
<p>&quot;The investor interest is very quiet, no-one's out buying long today,&quot; one Sydney-based dealer said.</p>
<p>At 0000 GMT (11.00 a.m.) June 90-day bank bill futures were down one point to 93.93.</p>
